The correct syntax for defining a function in Rust is as follows:

```rust
fn function_name(parameters) -> return_type {
    // function body
}
```

Here, `function_name` is the name of the function, `parameters` are the input parameters of the function, and `return_type` is the data type of the value returned by the function
